the president was hardly visible as he  departed for his weekend retreat at camp  david he left it to his spokesperson in  a statement to reiterate that he does  not regret his decision an orderly  drawdown is the phrase the  administration is sticking with  and yet on the ground in afghanistan the  white flag of the taliban and images  which show that every assumption made by  the americans was wrong from all corners  of the country videos emerging which  show the scale and speed of the taliban  advance this is kandahar in the south  support here for the taliban is  strongest and on a u.s military vehicle  they celebrated at a base in herat in  the far west fighters seized afghan  military equipment  and in logar province just south of the  capital the taliban released a whole  jail of prisoners  this isn't this isn't orderly it's kind  of hard to believe there can't be any  regret but there's no way i don't think  he can ever express that  i think president biden was elected into  office in part  to begin to withdraw from the so-called  forever wars and just listen to the  president a month ago is a taliban  takeover of afghanistan now inevitable  no  it is not it's taken just four weeks for  that statement to be proved so  spectacularly and alarmingly wrong it  was donald trump's policy to pull the  troops out joe biden adopted the  commitment believing it would play well  with voters here but the reality  thousands of miles away is now on him  the president and his advisers had  gambled that the taliban would stick to  commitments not to let al qaeda and  other terror groups return already  that's looking like wishful thinking  doug london is a former cia operations  officer and the u.s counterterrorism  chief covering afghanistan the taliban  and al-qaeda he says are literally  intermarried well i would not be  surprised to see  al-qaeda members moving back to  afghanistan from iran where many of them  sought refuge in sanctuary from  counter-terrorism pressure from the  united states the uk and others  and  basically taking advantage of the  opportunities to get back into the  business of training plotting and  planning and using the facilities of  afghanistan to project power outward  under the calmness of the kabul skyline  the fear and sense of betrayal cannot be  overstated the displacement camps are  filling and the 3 000 u.s troops who  will arrive here by the end of the  weekend cannot help their mission is  only to protect u.s civilians as that  orderly withdrawal is completed mark  stone sky news in washington
 

